"file":"preprints/The-Abelian-Zilber-Pink-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":43,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"31646d97ec0f2c4c5cbeb9991549e30a83cd08e34335323f39734c013aa97f48","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Abelian-Zilber-Pink-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:d2e521cc4cec9ffe94c2c414d4b4f13fe6bf6d3009fdf5feac3b970108c8f8c5","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Abelian-Zilber-Pink-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L43"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every number field $K$, every abelian variety $A/K$, and every\nirreducible subvariety $X\\subseteq A_{\\bar K}$, there are only finitely\nmany maximal atypical subvarieties of $X$ in\n$S=\\langle X\\rangle_{\\mathrm{sp}}$. Equivalently, there are finitely many\nproper atypical subvarieties $Y_1,\\ldots,Y_m\\subsetneq X$ such that every\natypical subvariety is contained in one of the $Y_j$."}
